From: LuneOS pioneer key-actions agent
Subject: [PATCH] Optionally open the notification panel with a fingerprint-sensor tap

A touch on the fingerprint sensor of an unlocked, lit phone opens the
notification panel, or closes it again, the way a tap on the minimised
notification icons does. Off by default behind a new tweak, "Fingerprint tap
opens notifications", and only with a finger enrolled.

Most fingerprint sensors have no navigation mode a shell could listen to:
the FPC1020 on the Xperia XA2 has none, and its interrupt only fires while
the HAL has armed it. So the touch is heard through an identify session with
com.webos.service.fingerprint, and any capture it reports, matched or not,
is a tap.

That session is the lock screen's own, extended to run while unlocked
(fingerprintListening = fingerprintActive || fingerprintTapActive), rather
than a second client: biomd refuses a second identify ("Another fingerprint
operation is in progress") and an abort from either client ends whichever session is running, so two
sessions racing each other on every lock and unlock would sooner or later
leave the lock screen deaf. With one session, locking simply makes the
session that was listening for taps mean "unlock". Unlocked captures never
count towards the lock screen's failed-attempt lockout, and for 1.5 s after
an unlock (and 0.8 s after each tap) captures are ignored, so the finger
that unlocked the phone does not also open the panel.

Two robustness fixes the tap mode needs, which also help unlock:
 - an identify the service refuses (returnValue false) is retried after 5 s
   instead of being ignored, which left the session dead;
 - a session that ends without a reply (another client's abort, or Settings
   enrolling a finger, pre-empts it silently) is noticed from getStatus
   going back to FPSTATE_IDLE and re-armed. While another client holds the
   sensor, tap mode waits for that rather than taking it back.

Tap mode is also off while Settings > Fingerprint is in front: biomd refuses
an enroll while an identify is pending ("Cannot perform this operation
while identification is in progress"), which is how enrolling first failed
while testing this on pioneer.

Costs: while the tweak is on the sensor stays armed whenever the screen is on
and unlocked, and a touch by an unenrolled finger is a failed match as far
as the HAL is concerned.

NotificationArea gains openNotificationArea() (what the tap on the icons
did) and toggleNotificationArea() for the new caller.

Upstream-Status: Pending
